IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nii-il04-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-schedule-j-tables`
IMPORT `nii-schedule-j`

-- TESTS EXPECTED TO FAIL, BY AN EXACT COUNT: 12 of the 52 assertions below (before 0.7.0: 15 of 41).
-- check.sh's `expected_failed` table names this module with 12, and encoding.json `expected_red`
-- says the same. A run with any other number of failures here is red.
--
-- CORRECTED 2026-11-09 (version 0.7.0; NOTES.md, "Correction 2026-11-09"). Until 0.6.1 this module's
-- first two families were its 14 failures: the consolidation's Schedule J has seven wrong cells
-- (four of them in both tables), so three of its columns did not add up to their printed totals
-- and the Institute's composites were not reached by the items. That was the CONSOLIDATION's
-- error: the official instruments print cells that sum exactly to their totals. With the official
-- cells encoded, families 1 and 2 are all satisfied (they stay here as the proof that the encoded
-- table adds up and agrees with the Institute); family 3, the one slip in an amending Act itself,
-- still fails; and family 4 is new: the consolidation's seven cells set against the official
-- ones, failing by design, so the discrepancy stays on record as a test.
--
-- 1. Each table of Schedule J ends with a totals row ("סך הכל"). Read as a total, each cell is the
--    sum of the figures printed above it. All nine columns of all four readings of the schedule
--    are checked: 36 assertions, ALL SATISFIED since 0.7.0 (10 failed until 0.6.1, when the
--    cells were the consolidation's: C above/employee 14.39 against 14.50 and 14.49 against 14.60;
--    C not above/employee, permanent, 4.16 against 3.85 and 4.26 against 3.95; D upper 4.67
--    against 7.00, in every reading).
--
-- 2. The National Insurance Institute's rate pages (fetched 2026-10-06; provenance in
--    nii-il04-published-figures.l4) print composite National Insurance rates for 2026 ABOVE the
--    reduced collection threshold: 4 assertions, ALL SATISFIED since 0.7.0 (they failed until
--    0.6.1, the items of the consolidation's cells not reaching them). They ask the items'
--    reading by name, so they compare the items with the Institute:
--      employee, all branches: 14.6% (items 14.60)
--      employee's deduction, all deduction branches: 7% (items 7.00)
--      controlling shareholder (form 102 "column 2"): 19.34% with health insurance at 5.17%,
--        so 14.17% National Insurance (items, without unemployment and insolvency:
--        14.60 - 0.37 - 0.06 = 14.17)
--      controlling shareholder's deduction: 11.96% with health insurance at 5.17%, so 6.79%
--        (items, without unemployment: 7.00 - 0.21 = 6.79)
--    The Institute's page therefore agrees with the OFFICIAL cells, which is independent
--    corroboration of the correction (its figures come from the Institute, not from the
--    consolidation or from the Sefer HaChukim pages the correction rests on).
--
-- 3. The 2025 text as enacted: 1 assertion, 1 expected to fail (below).
--
-- 4. The consolidation's seven wrong cells against the official ones: 11 assertions (seven in the
--    permanent table, four of the same cells in the temporary one), ALL 11 EXPECTED TO FAIL. Each
--    asserts that the figure the consolidation prints (typed from the quoted source line) equals
--    the figure the official instrument prints (the figure the encoding takes). They fail by
--    design: they are the record that the deposited consolidation is wrong there.

§ `Expected red`

`all nine figure columns` MEANS
    LIST `column C, above the threshold, employee`, `column C, above the threshold, self-employed`
       , `column C, above the threshold, neither`, `column C, not above the threshold, employee`
       , `column C, not above the threshold, self-employed`, `column C, not above the threshold, neither`
       , `column D, upper part of the wage`, `column D, part of the wage not above the threshold`, `column E`

