§§ `2. The Institute's composites above the threshold, 2026 — 4 assertions, all satisfied`

`the version for 2026` MEANS `Schedule J — the version for a contribution month in` 2026

`all nine branches` MEANS
    LIST `maternity`, `children`, `work injury`, `accident injury`, `unemployment`
       , `employees' rights in insolvency proceedings`, `disability`, `long-term care`
       , `senior citizens and survivors`

`the branches of a controlling shareholder who is an employee` MEANS
    LIST `maternity`, `children`, `work injury`, `accident injury`, `disability`, `long-term care`
       , `senior citizens and survivors`

`the branches with a deduction from the wage` MEANS
    LIST `maternity`, `accident injury`, `unemployment`, `disability`, `long-term care`
       , `senior citizens and survivors`

`health insurance on an employee above the threshold, as the Institute's page prints it` MEANS 5.17

GIVEN v  IS A `A version of Schedule J`
      c  IS A `A figure column of Schedule J`
      bs IS A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the combined column D percentage of` v `in` c `for` bs MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN b YIELD `the percentage in column D of` v `for` b `in` c) bs)

#ASSERT `the combined percentage in column C of` `the version for 2026` `for` `an employee` `,` `the part above the reduced collection threshold` `,` `in the branches` `all nine branches` `, at the items` EQUALS 14.6
#ASSERT `the combined column D percentage of` `the version for 2026` `in` `column D, upper part of the wage` `for` `the branches with a deduction from the wage` EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `the combined percentage in column C of` `the version for 2026` `for` `an employee` `,` `the part above the reduced collection threshold` `,` `in the branches` `the branches of a controlling shareholder who is an employee` `, at the items` EQUALS 19.34 MINUS `health insurance on an employee above the threshold, as the Institute's page prints it`
#ASSERT `the combined column D percentage of` `the version for 2026` `in` `column D, upper part of the wage` `for` (LIST `maternity`, `accident injury`, `disability`, `long-term care`, `senior citizens and survivors`) EQUALS 11.96 MINUS `health insurance on an employee above the threshold, as the Institute's page prints it`

§§ `3. The 2025 text as enacted — 3 assertions, 1 expected to fail (added 2026-10-07; the two passing ones added 2026-11-09)`

-- WHICH VALUE APPLIES WHEN (checked 2026-11-09 against the page images of both instruments). The cell
-- is 0.17 in calendar 2025: Amendment 252, s 7(a)(3)(a), Sefer HaChukim 3347, p. 177 (14.1.2025),
-- which also prints the column's total as 6.92. It is 0.16 from 1 January 2026: the 2025
-- budget-year Law, s 20(1), Sefer HaChukim 3384, p. 396 (27.3.2025), replaces "0.17" with "0.16" in
-- that table, and s 21 commences the chapter on 1 January 2026. The encoding answers 2026 on with
-- 0.16 (the version for 2026 on, family 1 above, where the column adds up to 6.92); the 2025 text is
-- kept only as data, with 0.17, and 2025 itself is declined (nii-schedule-j.l4).

-- Amendment 252 s 7(a)(3)(a) as enacted (Sefer HaChukim 3347, p. 177) prints item 2's lower figure
-- for those who are neither as 0.17 and the column's total as 6.92; the items sum to 6.93. The
-- 2025 budget-year Law s 20(1) (from 1 January 2026) made the figure 0.16, after which the column
-- meets its total (asserted, satisfied, in family 1 above for the 2026 readings). Expected to fail:
-- the 2025 text did not meet its own printed total.
-- The Knesset's own cure changed the item (0.17 to 0.16) and kept the printed total (6.92), which is
-- consistent with fork F4's default of letting the printed totals govern.
#ASSERT `the items sum to the printed total of` `Schedule J, the temporary version as enacted for 2025 (data; 2025 is not answered)` `in` `column C, not above the threshold, neither`

-- The slip, typed: the 2025 column's items sum to 6.93 and its printed total is 6.92.
#ASSERT `the sum of the items of` `Schedule J, the temporary version as enacted for 2025 (data; 2025 is not answered)` `in` `column C, not above the threshold, neither` EQUALS 6.93
#ASSERT `the printed total of` (`Schedule J, the temporary version as enacted for 2025 (data; 2025 is not answered)`'s `totals`) `in` `column C, not above the threshold, neither` EQUALS 6.92

§§ `4. The consolidation's seven wrong cells against the official ones — 11 assertions, all 11 expected to fail (added 2026-11-09)`

-- CORRECTED 2026-11-09. The Hebrew Wikisource consolidation prints seven cells that the official
-- text does not, four of them in both tables (NOTES.md, "Correction 2026-11-09"). Each assertion
-- below sets the figure the consolidation prints (typed from the quoted source line, the `src:`
-- line above it) against the figure the encoding takes from the official instrument (the page
-- images of Sefer HaChukim 2382 p. 756 and 2023 p. 813 are quoted on `ext:` lines at the head of
-- nii-schedule-j-tables.l4). The consolidation's figure is on the left; each assertion fails.
-- Where the wrong figures come from: column C above the threshold, employee, items 6, 7, 9 (0.33,
-- 0.04, 0.28) are the temporary text for 2014 (Sefer HaChukim 2429, p. 266, s 3(1)); column C not
-- above the threshold, employee, items 1, 3, 10 (0.16, 1.47, 1.67) are the interim text of 1 August
-- 2009 to 31 March 2011 (Sefer HaChukim 2203, p. 259, s 145(a)); column D upper, item 10, prints
-- 1.52, which is the official figure of column C not above, item 10, in the same 2005 table (the
-- cause of that one is not established). All three expired texts entered the consolidation in one
-- edit of 2023-05-31 (Hebrew Wikisource revision 2763716).

-- Permanent version.
-- src:4738 | 1. | אימהות | 1.40 | 0.94 | – | 0.16 | 0.24 | – | 0.87 | 0.04 | 0.09 |
#ASSERT (JUST 0.16) EQUALS `the cell of` `Schedule J (permanent version), item 1` `in` `column C, not above the threshold, employee`
-- src:4740 | 3. | ילדים | 2.08 | 2.74 | 1.67 | 1.47 | 0.59 | 1.10 | – | – | 0.08 |
#ASSERT (JUST 1.47) EQUALS `the cell of` `Schedule J (permanent version), item 3` `in` `column C, not above the threshold, employee`
-- src:4743 | 6. | אבטלה | 0.33 | – | – | 0.04 | – | – | 0.21 | 0.01 | 0.06 |
#ASSERT (JUST 0.33) EQUALS `the cell of` `Schedule J (permanent version), item 6` `in` `column C, above the threshold, employee`
-- src:4744 | 7. | זכויות עובדים בהליכי חדלות פירעון | 0.04 | – | – | 0.01 | – | – | – | – | 0.02 |
#ASSERT (JUST 0.04) EQUALS `the cell of` `Schedule J (permanent version), item 7` `in` `column C, above the threshold, employee`
-- src:4746 | 9. | סיעוד | 0.28 | 0.21 | 0.14 | 0.05 | 0.05 | 0.09 | 0.14 | 0.01 | 0.02 |
#ASSERT (JUST 0.28) EQUALS `the cell of` `Schedule J (permanent version), item 9` `in` `column C, above the threshold, employee`
